{# Decision template: the player's turn in a SexLab mini-game scene while the player is on auto play (HUD
   take-control key). The AI plays the player like an NPC: how they behave (strategy), whether they say something
   now, which HUD key they press (or none), and what they would pick in the Aid / Punish dialog boxes.
   Sent by SkyrimNet_SexLab.dll (StrategyDecision.cpp) through PublicSendCustomDecisionToLLM: when auto play turns
   on, at scene start, and after each line anyone in the player's scene speaks. Rendered into a decisions request,
   never into chat messages.

   Context pushed by the game (C++ snapshot): everything minigame_strategy.prompt gets (the player is the focus;
   no current strategy, timeline instead of recent dialogue),
   plus last_speaker (who said last_line_text, "" = the player), has_strategy, ask_speak, hotkeys [key, text],
   aid_options [key, text], punish_options [key, text], punish_methods [key, text], parts. Keys are read back by the
   game: keep {{ o.key }} as given. A criterion is one line. #}
{% set _focus = decnpc(focus_uuid) %}
[ state focus ]
{{ focus_name }}, {{ _focus.gender }} {{ _focus.race }}, is the {{ role }} in this scene{% if not expects_orgasm %} (this act is not expected to bring {{ focus_name }} to orgasm){% endif %}.
{{ focus_name }} is {{ arousal }}{% if orgasms > 0 %} and has climaxed {{ orgasms }} time{% if orgasms > 1 %}s{% endif %} so far{% endif %}.
{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", focus_uuid) }}
[ end state ]

[ state scene ]
{% set _sexlab = sexlab_get_threads(focus_uuid) %}
{% if existsIn(_sexlab, "threads") %}
{% for thread in _sexlab.threads %}
{% for actor_record in thread.actors %}
{% if to_number(actor_record.uuid) == focus_uuid %}
{% if existsIn(thread, "location") and thread.location != "" %}On {{ thread.location }}, {% endif %}{{ thread.description }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state partners ]
{% for p in partners %}
{{ p.name }}: the {{ p.role }}, {{ p.arousal }}{% if p.orgasms > 0 %}, climaxed {{ p.orgasms }} time{% if p.orgasms > 1 %}s{% endif %}{% endif %}. {{ focus_name }} and {{ p.name }} are {{ p.relationship }}.
- {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", p.uuid) }}
{% endfor %}
[ end state ]

[ state timeline ]
{% if length(timeline) > 0 %}
{% for line in timeline %}
{{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
Nothing has happened yet.
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state last_line ]
{% if trigger == "dialogue" and last_line_text != "" %}{% if last_speaker != "" %}{{ last_speaker }}{% else %}{{ focus_name }}{% endif %} just said: "{{ last_line_text }}"{% else %}Nothing has just been said; {{ focus_name }} is acting on their own.{% endif %}
[ end state ]

{% if has_strategy %}
[ question strategy choice ]
Decide which strategy {{ focus_name }} decides to start using right now.
Base it on their relationship with each partner (`partners`), what is happening (`scene`), and what {{ focus_name }} has thought, said and experienced (`timeline`).
In order of importance: `last_line`, {{ focus_name }}'s thoughts, and recent events over older events. {{ focus_name }}'s words are more about changing other people's behavior than describing {{ focus_name }}'s own desires.
A victim who is resisting does not cooperate. A lover or friend who is lagging behind may be helped. A rival or enemy is unlikely to be generous.
Passive only fits someone reluctant, exhausted or uninterested; a willing participant takes an active part.
[ criteria ]
{% for o in options %}
{{ o.key }}: {{ o.text }}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
{% endif %}

{% if ask_speak %}
[ question speak noul ]
Does {{ focus_name }} want to say something right now{% if trigger == "dialogue" and last_line_text != "" %}, in reply to `last_line`{% else %} in this moment{% endif %}?
Yes when {{ focus_name }} was addressed, has a strong reaction, or would naturally answer. No when {{ focus_name }} just spoke, has nothing to add, or would stay silent (a gagged, overwhelmed or sullen character).
[ end question ]
{% endif %}

[ question hotkey choice ]
Which of these does {{ focus_name }} do right now, if any? Most of the time the answer is `none`: act only when `last_line`, the scene or {{ focus_name }}'s character clearly calls for it.
Ending the scene is only for when {{ focus_name }} clearly wants it to stop or it has run its course.
[ criteria ]
{% for o in hotkeys %}
{{ o.key }}: {{ o.text }}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]

{% if length(aid_options) > 0 %}
[ question aid_option choice ]
If {{ focus_name }} chose `aid` (heal or restore someone), which spell or potion would they use, and on whom?
[ criteria ]
{% for o in aid_options %}
{{ o.key }}: {{ o.text }}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]

[ question aid_part choice ]
If {{ focus_name }} chose `aid`, where on the body would they apply it?
[ criteria ]
{% for p in parts %}
{{ p }}: {% if p == "body" %}nowhere in particular{% else %}the {{ p }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
{% endif %}

{% if length(punish_options) > 0 %}
[ question punish_option choice ]
If {{ focus_name }} chose `punish`, whom would they punish?
[ criteria ]
{% for o in punish_options %}
{{ o.key }}: {{ o.text }}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]

[ question punish_method choice ]
If {{ focus_name }} chose `punish`, how would they hurt them?
[ criteria ]
{% for o in punish_methods %}
{{ o.key }}: {{ o.text }}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]

[ question punish_part choice ]
If {{ focus_name }} chose `punish`, where on that person's body would they strike?
[ criteria ]
{% for p in parts %}
{{ p }}: {% if p == "body" %}nowhere in particular{% else %}the {{ p }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
{% endif %}
